  "visualBrief": "Complete connected Palais Bourbon parliamentary exterior: twelve-column river portico, tall solid blank/original pediment and broad stairs, rounded chamber roof, four-column ceremonial-court portico, both returned court wings, complete connected administrative/library ranges around all three actual courtyard holes, corner pavilions, mansard/dormer bands, open balustrades and closed recessed glazing/doors. Native north porch, court porch and south colonnade remain open between real columns. Separate Hôtel de Lassay frontage53, gallery52, ministries, city, gardens and artwork remain independent. No copied statuary, heraldry, lettering or interiors.",
